Aerie-Purpose: Round a restored Linux window by the Aerie token radius when the OS frame provider reports none, so the frame, its shadow and the tint share one radius.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_frame_view_linux_native.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #249. BrowserFrameViewLinuxNative took its corner radius only from the frame provider (the GTK
theme), so on a desktop whose theme gives no window radius (KDE Plasma) the window was square.
GetRestoredCornerRadiusDip() now asks aerie_frame::WindowCornerRadius() (components/aerie_frame):
the provider's radius as it is when it is non-zero, radius-xl when it is zero, square when the window
is maximised, fullscreen or tiled, or cannot draw transparent corners. "Can draw" is the base class's
own answer (a custom frame, no tiling, a compositor with translucency), so a bare Xvfb stays square.
PaintRestoredFrameBorder() uses the base class's painter, with the same radius and its shadow, when
the provider has no radius to paint with.


